# cogno-chain — environment surface (safe defaults; no secrets in this file).
#
# The all-Rust backend is one node + a run-anywhere CLI + a static frontend, so there are very few
# env vars. There are NO follower / relayer / indexer / committee services and NO signing seeds in
# env: the CLI reads no environment at all (keys go in BY FILE), and every privileged call goes
# through the committee (there is no sudo). The two shipped systemd units are both the same node
# binary — a validator and a public archive node — but only the validator is given DBSYNC_URL; see
# the node section below for why the archive node must never have it.
#
# Nothing auto-loads this file. It is the map; the per-component copies are what get read:
#   • node     — deploy/systemd/cogno.env.example → /etc/cogno/cogno.env (systemd EnvironmentFile)
#   • frontend — app/.env.example → app/.env.local (Next reads env files from app/, not the root)
# For a local node run, copy this to `.env` (gitignored) and `set -a; . ./.env`. The one thing that
# reads a repo-root `.env` on its own is `npm run psi` — see PAGESPEED_API_KEY at the bottom.

# ── node (cogno-chain-node) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read-only Cardano db-sync the in-protocol observer reads. Absent/unset ⇒ the observer abstains and
# the chain still produces + finalizes. MAINNET PREREQUISITE: FULL (non-pruned), tx_in-enabled (NOT
# --consumed-tx-out), over TLS.
#
# VALIDATOR ONLY. Every importing node re-derives its own observation for the blocks it imports, so a
# second db-sync that is behind, pruned, or on another network makes an archive/relay node compute a
# different answer than the validator did — a `ComputeDiverged` that is FATAL on import: it rejects
# the validator's perfectly valid blocks and freezes at the tip. With no db-sync it abstains and
# tracks the chain correctly. That is why deploy/systemd/cogno-relay.service ships with no
# EnvironmentFile at all, and why scripts/run-tracking-node.sh unsets both variables defensively.
#
# DBSYNC_URL and DBSYNC are the only two variables the node's own code reads, and DBSYNC is a
# fallback: both the observer's inherent write path and the boot-time config_check probe try
# DBSYNC_URL first, then DBSYNC. Prefer DBSYNC_URL; the alias exists so an inherited shell env still
# works. RUST_LOG is read by the SDK's logging layer rather than by anything in this repo, but it is
# honoured.
DBSYNC_URL=postgres://cogno_reader:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/cexplorer
# DBSYNC=
# RUST_LOG=info

# ── frontend (app/, inlined into the bundle at build) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical copy with the full commentary: app/.env.example. There are four NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars, all
# inlined by Next at build time and therefore PUBLIC. See app/README.md for the config table.

# The node JSON-RPC the SPA reads and writes through (PAPI). Unset ⇒ wss://cogno.forum/rpc, the live
# preprod chain, so a clean clone works with no configuration. A production build REFUSES a plain
# ws:// pointed at a public host (an https page mixed-content-blocks it); wss:// passes, and so does
# a loopback ws://127.0.0.1 / ws://localhost — which is why the sample below is a legal build value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:9944
# Preprod project id for the in-browser L1 vault lock/exit. Empty ⇒ the lock action is hidden.
# Exposed client-side by design: a visitor locks from their own wallet, with no backend in the path.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BLOCKFROST_PROJECT_ID=

# Operator serve denylist — what THIS deployment declines to render. It changes what the site shows
# and nothing about the chain; every node still serves the full record. Operator config, not user
# config: there is deliberately no Settings/localStorage override, in either direction. Ships EMPTY,
# and empty is a literal no-op. A malformed entry FAILS a production build rather than being quietly
# dropped, because a silently-ignored typo deploys green while still serving the content. See
# POLICY.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DENY_AUTHORS=                              # comma-separated ss58, prefix 42
NEXT_PUBLIC_DENY_POSTS=                                # comma-separated decimal post ids

# ── CIP-8 CI oracle (ci/cip8-oracle/, optional local run) ──────────────────────────────────
# The agreement test shells out to a headless MeshJS fixture (app/scripts/m2-cip8-fixture.mjs) — use
# the nvm node, not snap. Defaults are NODE_BIN=node (first on PATH) and APP_DIR=<repo>/app, so
# neither normally needs setting. Careful if you source this file into a shell:
# scripts/run-tracking-node.sh uses NODE_BIN for the built cogno-chain-node binary, not for Node.js.
# NODE_BIN=/home/you/.nvm/versions/node/v22.12.0/bin/node
# APP_DIR=/path/to/cogno-chain/app

# ── tooling credentials (never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never in the bundle) ──────────────────────────
# Google PageSpeed Insights key for `npm run psi` (app/scripts/psi.mjs), which audits the DEPLOYED
# site. It checks the environment, then app/.env.local, then this repo-root .env. Anonymous callers
# get 429.
# PAGESPEED_API_KEY=

# Other repo scripts (scripts/run-tracking-node.sh, scripts/acceptance, scripts/fetch-chainspec.mjs)
# take their own env fallbacks, documented in each script's header. scripts/check-metadata.sh is the
# exception: its NODE override is explained beside the code rather than in the header, and its
# SNAPSHOT / PORT knobs appear only in the source. All of them are per-invocation knobs rather than
# deployment config, so they are not listed here.
